{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113132","id":3041825622,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc61TpNW","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113132","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113132.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113132.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113132","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113132/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113132/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113132/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/5f7566a72ec265335b006a337287b976fd77e3fd","number":113132,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Reuse/optimize common `OperatorEvaluator*::evaluate` logic","user":{"login":"aaronp64","id":136198872,"node_id":"U_kgDOCB462A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/136198872?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronp64","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Added `CommonEvaluate` class to be used by `OperatorEvaluator*` classes that have the same logic for `evaluate` and `validated_evaluate`. `CommonEvaluate` initializes the return `Variant` to the correct type, then passes through to `validated_evaluate`, reducing code duplication between `evaluate`/`validated_evaluate` and avoiding the overhead of creating/destroying temporary `Variant`s from previous `evaluate` implementations.\r\n\r\nThe main performance benefit from this change is for methods that call `Variant::evaluate` directly, such as `sort` and `min`/`max` methods.  GDScript handling of operators already has some optimizations to use `VariantInternal::initialize`/`validated_evaluate` instead of `evaluate`, as long as the same operator expression continues to be called with the same `Variant` types.  If the types change, it will fall back to `evaluate`, which would be faster with this change.  The `sum_int` and `sum_float` benchmarks below are meant to show this case - `sum_int` uses `int`s when calculating the sum in `sum_array`, then `sum_float` calls `sum_array` using `float`s.\r\n\r\nCompared with gdscript below:\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nfunc _ready():\r\n\trun_test(\"sort_int\")\r\n\trun_test(\"sort_str\")\r\n\trun_test(\"min_max\")\r\n\trun_test(\"sum_int\")\r\n\trun_test(\"sum_float\")\r\n\trun_test(\"sort_dict\")\r\n\r\nfunc run_test(test_name: String):\r\n\tvar start := Time.get_ticks_msec()\r\n\tcall(test_name)\r\n\tvar end := Time.get_ticks_msec()\r\n\tprint(\"%s: %dms\" % [test_name.rpad(10), end - start])\r\n\r\nfunc sort_int():\r\n\tvar a := range(10000)\r\n\tfor i in 100:\r\n\t\ta.shuffle()\r\n\t\ta.sort()\r\n\r\nfunc sort_str():\r\n\tvar a := range(10000).map(str)\r\n\tfor i in 100:\r\n\t\ta.shuffle()\r\n\t\ta.sort()\r\n\r\nfunc min_max():\r\n\tvar a := range(10000)\r\n\tfor i in 1000:\r\n\t\ta.min()\r\n\t\ta.max()\r\n\r\nfunc sum_int():\r\n\tvar a := range(10000)\r\n\tfor i in 1000:\r\n\t\tsum_array(a)\r\n\r\nfunc sum_float():\r\n\tvar a := range(10000).map(func(i): return float(i))\r\n\tfor i in 1000:\r\n\t\tsum_array(a)\r\n\r\nfunc sum_array(a):\r\n\tvar s = 0\r\n\tfor n in a:\r\n\t\ts += n\r\n\treturn s\r\n\r\nfunc sort_dict():\r\n\tvar d := {}\r\n\tfor i in 10000:\r\n\t\td[str(i)] = i\r\n\tfor i in 1000:\r\n\t\td.sort()\r\n```\r\n\r\nold:\r\n```\r\nsort_int  : 205ms\r\nsort_str  : 283ms\r\nmin_max   : 224ms\r\nsum_int   : 284ms\r\nsum_float : 363ms\r\nsort_dict : 106ms\r\n```\r\n\r\nnew:\r\n```\r\nsort_int  : 126ms\r\nsort_str  : 231ms\r\nmin_max   : 111ms\r\nsum_int   : 286ms\r\nsum_float : 326ms\r\nsort_dict : 80ms\r\n```\r\n<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch in priority.\r\n\r\nRelevant fixes are cherry-picked for stable branches as needed by maintainers.\r\n\r\nTo speed up the contribution process and avoid CI errors, please set up pre-commit hooks locally:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/guidelines/code_style.html\r\n-->\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3240950060,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMjQwOTUwMDYw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/performance","name":"performance","description":"","color":"447777","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12939969,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AxXLB","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/23","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23/labels","number":23,"state":"closed","title":"4.6","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_u